{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-182", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-01-festus-arrival", "grade": "B", "note": "Names Festus's assumption of the procuratorship under Nero; the three-day journey up to Jerusalem is the narrative's own detail."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-182", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-agrippa-ii-king", "grade": "A", "note": "'both king Agrippa, and principally Festus the procurator, were much displeased' - Agrippa II is 'king' alongside Festus's procuratorship."}
{"from": "text:josephus-war-2-271", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-24-27-festus-succeeded", "grade": "A", "note": "'Now it was that Festus succeeded Felix as procurator' - the War's independent notice of the same succession."}
{"from": "artifact:festus-coins", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-24-27-festus-succeeded", "grade": "B", "note": "Bronze prutahs attributed to Festus's mint carry Nero's name (NEP WNOC / KAICAPOC, year LE = 58/59); they attest the mint under his governorship, not his name."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-103", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-02-ananias-high-priest", "grade": "D", "note": "Josephus names Ananias son of Nebedeus high priest (appointed under Herod of Chalcis) - the traditional identification; but Ismael ben Fabus held the office 58-62 (see the complicates edge), when Festus governed, so the identification of Acts 25's high priest is disputed."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-159", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-agrippa-ii-king", "grade": "A", "note": "Nero 'bestowed on Agrippa a certain part of Galilee, Tiberias, and Tarichae... He gave him also Julias, a city of Perea, with fourteen villages' and ordered submission to his jurisdiction - Agrippa II as a ruling king in the 50s."}
{"from": "artifact:agrippa-ii-coins", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-agrippa-ii-king", "grade": "A", "note": "Coins with the Greek inscription ΒΑΣΙΛΕΩΣ ΑΓΡΙΠΠΟΥ ('King Agrippa') and, from 66 CE, his own bust name Agrippa II as king."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-145-147", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-bernice-herodian-queen", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus names Berenice, reports the talk about her living with her brother Agrippa, and her marriage to Polemo of Cilicia - the Herodian royal sister of Acts 25:13."}
{"from": "text:tacitus-histories-2-2", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-bernice-herodian-queen", "grade": "A", "note": "Tacitus calls her 'Queen Berenice', loved by Titus - an independent Roman witness to the same person."}
{"from": "artifact:berenice-athens-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-bernice-herodian-queen", "grade": "A", "note": "An Athenian honorific statue inscription of 61 CE calls Berenice basilissa ('queen') - within two years of the Acts 25 scene."}
{"from": "artifact:berenice-beirut-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-bernice-herodian-queen", "grade": "A", "note": "The Latin Beirut inscription calls her regina ('queen'), her name preceding her brother Agrippa's."}
{"from": "artifact:berenice-beirut-inscription", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-13-agrippa-ii-king", "grade": "A", "note": "The same Beirut inscription names her brother Agrippa, whose name follows hers - the royal pair of Acts 25:13 in stone."}
{"from": "text:pliny-epistles-10-96", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-11-appeal-right", "grade": "B", "note": "Pliny (c. 112 CE): accused who do not recant are executed, 'or, if they are Roman citizens, orders them to be taken to Rome' - the citizen's path to the emperor's tribunal in practice."}
{"from": "text:digest-48-6-7", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-11-appeal-right", "grade": "B", "note": "The lex Julia de vi publica made liable the magistrate who 'civem romanum adversus provocationem necaverit verberaverit' (killed or flogged a Roman citizen against his appeal) - the legal protection behind 'no one can give me up'."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-19-346", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-23-great-pomp", "grade": "C", "note": "Agrippa I entering the Caesarea theater in a silver garment that 'shone out after a surprising manner' shows Herodian royal display at the same city a generation earlier - context, not the 59/60 entry itself."}
{"from": "site:caesarea-maritima", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-25-06-judgment-seat", "grade": "B", "note": "The excavated Roman capital where the procurators resided and held court - the city where Festus sat on the bema; the judgment-seat structure itself is not identified."}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-179", "type": "complicates", "to": "claim:ac-25-02-ananias-high-priest", "note": "King Agrippa gave the high priesthood to Ismael son of Fabi, and the fetched Wikipedia list gives Ishmael II ben Fabus 58-62 - the high priest when Festus governed - against identifying Acts 25's 'high priest' with Ananias."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-27-festus-succeeded", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-porcius-festus", "note": "Extra verbatim source kept from the merged claim claim:ac-25-01-festus-procurator (Wikipedia's Porcius Festus page)."}
